# Local virtualenv for the toolchain — never committed (see requirements.txt).
.venv/

# Python bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch output from run_fixture.py --check goes to the system temp dir,
# but ignore any stray local output dir just in case.
fixtures/_out/

# mapgen/derived/ holds generated artifacts. Most of it is a QA/preview render
# (preview_*, qa_*, ...) regenerable on demand and kept out of the repo. The
# committed deliverables are listed explicitly:
#   land_sea_mask.png         the coastline authority (S2); S3b cuts provinces from it
#   state_labels.png          the state-cell partition (S3a); S3b's direct input
#   state_labels_index.json   per-cell macro / area / coastal flag / provisional key
#   COVERAGE.md               the achieved-vs-target density report
# The two rasters and the index are consumed by later phases, so they have to
# travel with the repo; COVERAGE.md is the record of where the sources fall short.
derived/*
!derived/land_sea_mask.png
# The inland-lake mask (board #3742), the companion generate_coastline_mask.py
# --from-fill emits beside land_sea_mask.png. Committed because the province and
# arable (#4921) pipelines both read it as a live input (sea = ~land & ~lake); a
# clone missing it would silently regenerate a different raster. Regenerate,
# never hand-edit.
!derived/lake_mask.png
!derived/state_labels.png
!derived/state_labels_index.json
!derived/COVERAGE.md
# The sea-zone layer (S3a, board #2593), generated by generate_sea_zones.py from
# the mask + the hand-drawn sea_zones source; the bootable-map milestone turns it
# into sea provinces + 99_seas.txt + default.map sea_starts.
!derived/sea_zones.png
!derived/sea_zones_index.json
# The first-pass province index (board #2773), generated by generate_provinces.py
# alongside map_data/provinces.png. Committed as the per-province record (id band,
# colour, area, coastal, impassable); the review renders (provinces_*_review.png)
# stay ignored — they embed the source globe pixels.
!derived/provinces_index.json
# The land region -> province grouping (board #2928), generated by
# generate_provinces.py from subdivide's reg_of. Region-keyed, the land mirror of
# sea_zones_index.json; committed so the bootable-map milestone (#2930) emits land
# state_regions/*.txt from it. provinces.png / provinces_index.json stay untouched.
!derived/land_regions_index.json
# The hub anchor -> seeded-province index (board #3665), generated by
# generate_provinces.py when mapgen/config/hub_worksheet.json exists. Committed as
# the single anchor->province authority: generate_land_regions.py picks hubs from
# it and validate_map.py (full) checks them against it. Absent when no worksheet.
!derived/hub_anchors_index.json
# The canon-river index (board #3703), generated by generate_rivers.py from the
# traced cyan network. Committed as the per-river record (name -> mouth, length,
# width, state keys) that #3677/#3687/#2968 consume. Written in Phase B once a
# real map_data/rivers.png ships; the rivers_preview.png render stays ignored
# (it embeds the source globe pixels).
!derived/rivers_index.json
# The land STATE-number identity index (board #4188), generated by
# generate_land_regions.py, read read-only by render_land_regions_preview.py.
# Committed so a regen can match the current region cut against the numbers
# already shipped in map_data/state_regions/*.txt instead of renumbering every
# region fresh each run (the province-id mirror of #3705). Never hand-edit —
# regenerate through generate_land_regions.py, or seed it once with
# mapgen/seed_land_state_ids.py.
!derived/land_state_ids.json
# The staged sea-region emit (board #2698), generated by generate_sea_regions.py
# from sea_zones_index.json. Committed so the bootable-map milestone consumes it
# verbatim (same rationale as sea_zones.png); it is NOT loaded by the game and is
# NOT in map_data/. The seas_named_review.png render stays ignored — it embeds the
# source globe pixels, like seas_partition_review.png.
!derived/seas_99_seas.txt
!derived/seas_sea_starts.txt

# derived/named/ is the S3a-2 review deliverable from render_named_map.py
# --tiles: flat-tinted state cells drawn from our own pixels only (no source
# art), so — unlike the rest of derived/ — it is meant to be committed.
!derived/named/
!derived/named/*.png

# The arable-potential heatmap (board #4921), generated by
# generate_arable_heatmap.py from the committed priors + mapgen/config/arable_lore.json.
# Committed as the shared physical+lore prior the epic's realm children (#3679-#3686)
# sample, plus its provenance sidecar (factor weights, normalization, histogram).
# Regenerate, never hand-edit; the arable_on_globe.png QA render stays ignored (it
# embeds the source globe pixels).
!derived/arable_heatmap.png
!derived/arable_heatmap_index.json

# The city-dot -> province record (board #3704), emitted by generate_provinces.py when
# impassable paint exists; validate_map._check_impassable_land reads it to prove every
# city is passable and reachable. Regenerate, never hand-edit.
!derived/canon_city_provinces_index.json
